        "response": {
          "output": "The graph has six note types: **incident**, **entity**, **pattern**, **lesson**, **decision** and **delivery**.\n\n- **incident:** one handled defect or investigation, keyed by ticket id. Symptom, root cause and resolution sit in frontmatter fields.\n- **entity:** a durable thing incidents happen to, such as a service, platform, component or team.\n- **pattern:** a recurring failure shape that generalizes across incidents.\n- **lesson:** a measured practice improvement, written by evidence-producing workflows like EDD runs.\n- **decision:** a settled, ADR-shaped technical choice keyed by a slug. Its `status` says whether it is still in force.\n- **delivery:** one shipped feature, fix or task. It is the counterpart of an incident.\n\nI read this from `skills/vault-graphrag/SKILL.md` in the main checkout at `/Users/mferecal/Code/claude-toolkit`. I couldn't reach your worktree at `/private/tmp/b5`, because the Grep, Glob and shell tools are disabled here and the IDE tools only see the main checkout. So this may differ slightly from `feat/edd-batch-5`. The per-type frontmatter contracts are in `references/schema.md`, which I haven't read."
