        "response": {
          "output": "No. Recall is the read path. It only writes the `prior-incidents.md` artifact and never touches incident notes.\n\nIf you mean vault-update, that upserts by ticket id. A re-run updates the existing note's fields in place, such as status or added links. It never creates a second note for the same ticket.\n\nIf you do see a duplicate incident note for that ticket, something broke the upsert key. Check that the basename matches the ticket id exactly."
